---
// Microbenchmark compiler dead-code elimination lie vs Sink variable + ResetTimer discipline.
const W = 900;
const H = 266;
---
<figure class="ge6c">
  <div class="ge6c-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Comparing a broken microbenchmark whose result is deleted by Go compiler dead-code elimination versus a reliable benchmark storing output to a package sink after ResetTimer.">
      {/* Left: Broken benchmark */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="424" height="238" rx="10" class="ge6c-card is-red" />
      <text x="30" y="40" class="ge6c-h-red">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Broken benchmark: compiler deletes the work</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Benchmark ảo: compiler xóa luôn đoạn code cần đo</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="56" width="392" height="94" rx="6" class="ge6c-box" />
      <text x="44" y="78" class="ge6c-b">func BenchmarkBad(b *testing.B) {'{'}</text>
      <text x="44" y="96" class="ge6c-m">  setupBigFixture() // counted inside timing!</text>
      <text x="44" y="114" class="ge6c-m">  for i := 0; i &lt; b.N; i++ {'{'}</text>
      <text x="44" y="132" class="ge6c-red">    _ = computeMask(0xab, uint64(i)) // unused!</text>
      <text x="44" y="146" class="ge6c-b">{'} }'} </text>

      <rect x="30" y="162" width="392" height="74" rx="6" class="ge6c-box is-red" />
      <text x="44" y="184" class="ge6c-b-red">0.31 ns/op · 0 B/op (Fake zero-cost speedup!)</text>
      <text x="44" y="204" class="ge6c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Inlining sees computeMask result is dropped and deletes it.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Compiler thấy kết quả không ai dùng nên cắt bỏ hẳn lời gọi.</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="44" y="220" class="ge6c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Always assert correctness on real outputs inside the test!</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Nên kiểm tra đúng/sai kết quả trước khi tin vào số đo tốc độ.</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right: Reliable benchmark */}
      <rect x="462" y="14" width="424" height="238" rx="10" class="ge6c-card is-ok" />
      <text x="478" y="40" class="ge6c-h-ok">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. Reliable benchmark: isolate setup + observe result</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Benchmark chuẩn: tách setup và ghi vào biến Sink</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="478" y="56" width="392" height="94" rx="6" class="ge6c-box" />
      <text x="492" y="78" class="ge6c-b">var Sink uint64 // package-level sink</text>
      <text x="492" y="96" class="ge6c-ok">setupBigFixture(); b.ResetTimer(); b.ReportAllocs()</text>
      <text x="492" y="114" class="ge6c-m">for i := 0; i &lt; b.N; i++ {'{'}</text>
      <text x="492" y="132" class="ge6c-m">  acc += computeMask(0xab, uint64(i))</text>
      <text x="492" y="146" class="ge6c-ok">{'}'} ; Sink = acc // forces real execution</text>

      <rect x="478" y="162" width="392" height="74" rx="6" class="ge6c-box is-ok" />
      <text x="492" y="184" class="ge6c-b-ok">0.61 ns/op + Run -count=6..10 &amp; check with benchstat</text>
      <text x="492" y="204" class="ge6c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Tip (Go 1.24+): for b.Loop() replaces b.N loops and</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Mẹo (Go 1.24+): dùng while b.Loop() giúp tự bỏ qua</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="492" y="220" class="ge6c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>blocks dead-code elimination around loop bodies automatically.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>thời gian setup và giữ compiler không xóa thân vòng lặp.</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Microbenchmarks lie fast when setup runs inside the timed region or the compiler eliminates unused return values. Export results to a package-level Sink variable (or use Go 1.24's b.Loop()) and inspect allocation bytes alongside ns/op.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Microbenchmark rất dễ ra số ảo nếu dính thời gian setup hoặc bị compiler tối ưu xóa mất hàm không dùng kết quả. Luôn ResetTimer, gắn kết quả vào biến Sink (hoặc b.Loop()) và đọc cả B/op lẫn allocs/op.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .ge6c { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .ge6c-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .ge6c svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .ge6c text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .ge6c-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .ge6c-card.is-red { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .ge6c-card.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge6c-card.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge6c-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .ge6c-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); }
  .ge6c-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge6c-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge6c-h-red { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .ge6c-h-ok { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge6c-h-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge6c-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .ge6c-b-red, .ge6c-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .ge6c-b-ok, .ge6c-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge6c-b-ok, :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge6c-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge6c-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .ge6c figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
